  "definition": "Sampling is a systematic procedure for transforming inputs into an output or decision in Statistical Inference. It is used in Data Collection, Experimentation, Survey Estimation. It is commonly considered alongside Confidence Interval, Sampling Distribution, Standard Error.",
  "intuition": "Use a carefully chosen subset to learn about a wider population while tracking selection uncertainty.",
  "mathematical_foundation": "\u2023 Likelihood Weighted Sampling \u25b8 Sampling Process (topological order), initially set weight = 1 \u25b8 Sampling probability of likelihood weighted sample \u2023 \ud835\udc46 \ud835\udc9b, \ud835\udc86 = \u03c2 \ud835\udc43(\ud835\udc67 |\ud835\udc43\ud835\udc4e\ud835\udc5f\ud835\udc52\ud835\udc5b\ud835\udc61\ud835\udc60(\ud835\udc4d )) through weighted sampling \u25b8 Is likelihood weighting better than rejection sampling?",
  "advantages": [
